{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lyric type represents text underlays for lyrics. Two text elements that are not separated by an elision"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element are part of the same syllable, but may have different text formatting. The MusicXML XSD is more strict"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the DTD in enforcing this by disallowing a second syllabic element unless preceded by an elision element."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The lyric number indicates multiple lines, though a name can be used as well. Common name examples are verse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and chorus."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Justification is center by default; placement is below by default. Vertical alignment is to the baseline of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the text and horizontal alignment matches justification. The print-object attribute can override a note’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"print-lyric attribute in cases where only some lyrics on a note are printed, as when lyrics for later verses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are printed in a block of text rather than with each note. The time-only attribute precisely specifies which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lyrics are to be sung which time through a repeated section."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"code":"<lyric>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/docu